  "goodToKnow": "Hindurch means through or throughout, and it usually comes after the expression: die ganze Nacht hindurch (all night long), jahrelang hindurch, Jahrhunderte hindurch. With places, it reinforces durch: durch den Wald hindurch (right through the forest). It's also used in separable verbs: hindurchgehen, hindurchsehen. Hin- shows direction away from the speaker, as in hinaus and hinein."
